WHAT THIS IS

This source code is published so that Erovoutika's students, trainees and
customers can read it, learn from it, and understand exactly what the app on
their phone does. That is the whole reason the repository is public.

It is NOT open source, and publishing it grants no licence beyond what is
written below.


YOU MAY

  - Read, study and reference this source code for personal learning.
  - Build and run it on your own device for your own private, non-commercial
    use, including with your own robot hardware.
  - Quote short excerpts in coursework, tutorials or discussion, with
    attribution to Erovoutika.
  - Adapt the bundled Arduino sketches under arduino_sketches/ and
    arduino_code_guide/ for your own robots, freely and without attribution.
    They are teaching material and are meant to be modified.

YOU MAY NOT, without prior written permission from Erovoutika

  - Publish, distribute or sell this application, or any derivative of it, on
    Google Play, the App Store, or any other distribution channel.
  - Use the Erovoutika name, logo, brand marks, product photography or product
    catalogue in any application, product or promotional material.
  - Use this code, in whole or in part, in a commercial product or service.
  - Remove or alter this notice.


